  "answer": "To declare and validate query parameters in FastAPI, you can create a Pydantic model that represents the structure and validation requirements of your query parameters. Here's how you can do it:\n\n```Python\nfrom fastapi import FastAPI, Query\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\nclass QueryParamsModel(BaseModel):\n    q1: str\n    q2: str\n\n@app.get(\"/items/\")\nasync def read_items(q1: str = Query(None, min_length=3, max_length=50),\n                      q2: str = Query(None, min_length=3, max_length=50)):\n    return {\"q1\": q1, \"q2\": q2}\n```\n\nThis example is supported by [tutorial/query-param-models-0].",
